---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { INSTALL_CHROME, RELEASES } from '../lib/links';
---
<Base
  title="Pricing · Datawake"
  description="Datawake is free forever. Pro adds deeper tools and is coming soon. No trial, no credit card needed for the free plan."
>

<Nav />

<!-- ─── PAGE HERO ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<div class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <h1>Simple, honest pricing</h1>
    <p>The core features are free, forever. Pro gives you deeper tools: more detail, more history, and alerts when things change. No trial. No credit card for the free plan.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ─── PRICING CARDS ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container pricing-inner">

    <div class="pricing-cards">

      <!-- Free -->
      <div class="pricing-card">
        <div class="pricing-badge">Free</div>
        <div class="pricing-name">Always free</div>
        <div class="pricing-amount">
          <span class="price">€0</span>
          <span class="period">/ forever</span>
        </div>
        <p class="pricing-desc">Everything you need to understand who's tracking you and what they're doing with your data.</p>
        <div class="pricing-divider"></div>
        <ul class="pricing-list">
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Says no to cookie banners for you</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Violation detection: catches sites that track you after Reject</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Report sites to your data protection authority</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Real-time tracker detection on every page</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Company names and what each tracker does</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Session recording alerts (Hotjar, Clarity, FullStory)</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Whether trackers sell or share your data</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Who's following you across multiple sites</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Ad interest profile based on your browsing</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Data breach check for your email</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>GDPR access and deletion letters, export as JSON</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="pricing-cta">
          <a href={INSTALL_CHROME} class="btn btn-primary" style="width:100%; justify-content:center;" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-install>
            <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-4"/><polyline points="7 10 12 15 17 10"/><line x1="12" y1="15" x2="12" y2="3"/></svg>
            Install free
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Pro -->
      <div class="pricing-card featured">
        <div class="pricing-badge">Pro</div>
        <div class="pricing-name">Datawake Pro</div>
        <div class="pricing-amount">
          <span class="price" style="font-size:22px;letter-spacing:-0.01em">Coming soon</span>
        </div>
        <p class="pricing-desc">Everything in the free plan, plus deeper tools for people who want to understand and act on their data footprint. Follow the project to hear when it launches.</p>
        <div class="pricing-divider"></div>
        <ul class="pricing-list">
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Everything in the free plan</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Full data broker exposure report (30+ brokers)</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Breach monitoring alerts when your email appears in a new breach</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Ready-to-send opt-outs for data brokers</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Weekly privacy activity digest</li>
          <li><span class="pcheck"><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6l3 3 5-5"/></svg></span>Early access to new features</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="pricing-cta">
          <a href={RELEASES} class="btn btn-mint" style="width:100%; justify-content:center;" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Follow on GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p style="text-align:center; margin-top:20px; font-size:13.5px; color:var(--text-muted);">
      Pro is in development. New releases are announced on GitHub.
    </p>

  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── FAQ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div style="text-align:center; margin-bottom:56px;">
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-bottom:0;">Questions we get a lot</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-list" id="faq">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Is the free plan really free forever?
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes. We'll never put a time limit on the free plan or require a credit card to use it. Core features (tracker detection, history, breach check, ad profile) are free with no catch. Pro is for people who want more, not a way to pressure you into paying.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Do you see my browsing history?
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          No. All data stays on your device, in your browser's local storage. The extension doesn't make network requests to our servers, so we physically cannot see the sites you've visited or the trackers you've encountered.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          How does the breach check work without sending my email to you?
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          The breach check is powered by Have I Been Pwned (HIBP), a trusted service run by security researcher Troy Hunt. You provide your own HIBP API key (HIBP charges for keys). When you check an email, the request goes directly from your browser to HIBP. We never see your email address.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Can I cancel Pro anytime?
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes, any time. No notice period, no questions asked. Your Pro access continues until the end of the billing month you've paid for. After that, you go back to the free plan and all your locally stored data stays intact.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Is the extension really open source?
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          Yes. The extension source code is on GitHub under the AGPL-3.0 licence. You (or anyone you trust) can read exactly what it does, what requests it makes, and where data goes. Privacy tools should be verifiable, not just trustworthy on our word.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question">
          Does Datawake slow down my browser?
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          In normal use, no. Datawake observes the requests your browser is already making and adds no requests of its own. It runs a few small scripts on each page to read the cookie banner and spot fingerprinting, without changing what the page does. Data is stored in IndexedDB, your browser's built-in database, which is fast and doesn't affect page rendering.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-question').forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const item = btn.closest('.faq-item');
      const wasOpen = item?.classList.contains('open');
      document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item').forEach((i) => i.classList.remove('open'));
      if (!wasOpen) item?.classList.add('open');
    });
  });
</script>

<Footer />

</Base>
